---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Testimonial from '../components/Testimonial.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Form from '../components/Form.astro';
import Field from '../components/Field.astro';
import Badge from '../components/Badge.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="imagi for Families: Coding and AI Projects for Kids"
  description="Your child builds real games and projects with code and AI, safely. Guided projects for ages 8 and up, with everything you need to see what they are making."
>
  <section class="hero hero--subtle">
    <div class="hero_inner">
      <div class="hero_text">
        <Badge tone="dark">For parents</Badge>
        <h1 class="text-display-l">The AI creation platform schools use, now coming home</h1>
        <div class="hero_lead text-body-l">
          <p>
            Teachers use imagi to help students build with AI in a safe, compliant space. Soon kids 8 and up can keep creating at home, and
            you’ll be able to see everything they make.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero_actions">
          <Button href="https://410q0v.share-na2.hsforms.com/2m7asWYPLRUagLS9QypbztA" size="l" arrow external
            >Join the family waitlist</Button
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--page">
    <div class="section_inner">
      <header class="section-header">
        <h2 class="text-display-s">Kids learn to build with AI</h2>
        <div class="section-header_intro text-body-l">
          <p>
            Kids 8 and up use real-world AI tools, like the app builder Lovable, in a space made for them. They learn to use AI to make
            their own work, not to do the work for them, and they build skills they'll use well beyond school.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <Card icon="tablet" title="Screen time that makes something">
          <p>
            Instead of watching another video, your child writes a few lines of code and ends up with pixel art, an animation or a small
            game they designed themselves.
          </p>
        </Card>
        <Card icon="brain" iconTone="accent" title="Building with AI, not cheating with it">
          <p>
            Your child describes an app they want, AI builds a first version, and then the real work starts. They test it, find what is
            broken and fix it. They finish understanding what the AI actually did.
          </p>
        </Card>
        <Card icon="laptop" iconTone="brand" title="Real code, not a toy version">
          <p>
            Your child learns Python, the language used in real jobs. No colorful blocks they will have to outgrow in a couple of years.
          </p>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--subtle">
    <div class="section_inner">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split_text">
          <h2 class="text-display-s">How it works at home</h2>
          <h3 class="text-heading-m">Starting is easier than you think</h3>
          <p class="text-body-l text-secondary">
            Start with the free coding game. It runs on iPhone and iPad, costs nothing, and needs no experience. Ages 8 and up.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-l text-secondary">
            When your child wants more, imagi Edu gives them safe access to real AI tools like Lovable, inside an account you set up. You
            see every prompt and everything they build, and no personal data is collected.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-l text-secondary">
            Homeschooling? imagi can often count as an approved STEM expense under state Education Savings Account programs.
          </p>
          <Button href="https://410q0v.share-na2.hsforms.com/2m7asWYPLRUagLS9QypbztA" arrow external>Join the waitlist</Button>
        </div>
        <div class="split_media">
          <img class="split_image"
            src="/images/for-parents/5_3f5973aa-49ff-4daa-a1f7-2e190e0270ea_480x480.webp"
            alt="Two children coding pixel art on a laptop together"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--page">
    <div class="section_inner">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split_text">
          <h2 class="text-display-s">Try imagi for free</h2>
          <p class="text-body-l text-secondary">
            Download the imagi coding game for at-home use and let kids ages 8-14+ learn coding independently.
          </p>
          <a class="appstore" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/imagi-fun-coding-game/id1434239482" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <img class="appstore_badge" src="/images/for-parents/appstorebtn.png" alt="Download imagi on the App Store" />
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="split_media split_media--first">
          <img class="split_image"
            src="/images/for-parents/the_easiest_way_to_learn_coding_with_a_coding_app_for_kids_1.png"
            alt="Three phone screens from the imagi coding game: lessons, Python code and pixel-art projects"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted">
    <div class="section_inner">
      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <Testimonial name="Kelly Powers" role="CS Teacher, Private School - NY, USA" image="/images/computer-science/kelly-p.jpeg">
          You have something special - a rigorous and engaging curriculum where students are passionate about creating projects with code
          and sharing those projects.
        </Testimonial>
        <Testimonial name="Mr. Godinez" role="Academy of IT, Florida" image="/images/computer-science/1619653945474.jpeg">
          Through imagi, students learn that their first attempt doesn't always work, and that's the point. It teaches them to refine their
          instructions and think critically about coding and AI.
        </Testimonial>
        <Testimonial
          name="Paige Besthoff"
          role="Computer Science Teacher, Public School - Spotswood, NJ"
          image="/images/computer-science/1644789063101.jpeg"
        >
          You don’t have to know anything about teaching computer science. After the PD our art, math and reading teachers were all able to
          incorporate the imagi platform into their curriculum. There are so many cross-curricular opportunities available.
        </Testimonial>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--page">
    <div class="section_inner">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="split_text">
          <h2 class="text-display-s">Pick your starting point</h2>
          <p class="text-body-l text-secondary">Check out our collection of products!</p>
          <Button href="https://imagilabs.com/collections/all" arrow>Shop now</Button>
        </div>
        <div class="split_media"><img class="split_image" src="/images/for-parents/imagi-product1.webp" alt="The imagiCharm in its box" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--subtle">
    <div class="section_inner section_inner--narrow">
      <header class="section-header">
        <h2 class="text-display-s">Let's keep in touch</h2>
        <div class="section-header_intro text-body-l">
          <p>Join our newsletter for updates, discounts & resources for the classroom and beyond!</p>
        </div>
      </header>
      <Form submitLabel="Sign up to our newsletter">
        <Field label="Email" name="email" type="email" placeholder="Your email" required full />
      </Form>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .appstore {
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .appstore_badge {
    height: 56px;
    width: auto;
  }
</style>
